## Context
Epic Cults. Agents reach the desktop through `dm` core commands that call `core.desktopClient` over `DM_DESKTOP_PIPE`, as `nameChat` does (`src/core/commands/chatNaming.ts` → `src/core/desktop/desktopClient.ts` → `src/main/naming/controlPipe.ts`). Add cult commands the same way.

## Change
- Core commands, in `src/core/commands/cults.ts` with capabilities in `src/core/commands/capabilities.ts` and `src/core/authz.ts`:
  - Magos only: `summon_acolyte {name?, mission, model?, tierReason?}`, `dismiss_acolyte {name}`, `list_acolytes {}` (names, models, states), `petition {kind: 'acolytes'|'allow_save'|'folder_access', additional?, folder?, reason}`, `conclude_run {chronicle}`, and **`order_all {body}`** (revision 3).
  - Both roles: `cult_status {}` (own name, Magos name, state, remaining time or unlimited, cap, pending petitions).
  - Acolyte only: `conclude_service {report}`.
  - camelCase aliases follow the registry.
- Generalize the control pipe to carry these operations alongside naming, keeping its framing, size limits and deadline. Main resolves the **caller from the bound grant → chat → cult membership**. Arguments never name a run, a role or a sender. A non-member gets `unauthorized`.
- Rules enforced in main through `cultSupervisor`:
  - a summon defaults to `cheapest(ompModels)`; a missing name is generated, and a taken name is refused with `name_taken`;
  - a model not in the signed-in list is refused with the available ids;
  - a tier above the cheapest requires a non-empty `tierReason`, stored on the member;
  - cap and state refusals are typed;
  - `conclude_run` stores the chronicle (inert text, at most 32 KiB) and starts the end of the run.
- `order_all {body}` (revision 3: the chamber animates it as one broadcast):
  - main sends one mailbox message from the Magos's own endpoint to each live acolyte of its run, through the comms mailbox service on the same path, size limits and wake rules as `send_agent_message`;
  - main records one `cult_events` row `{kind: 'order_all', orderId, messageIds, recipients}`;
  - it is refused with `no_acolytes` when there are none, `run_paused` while paused and `run_ending` while ending;
  - it returns the orderId and the recipient names.
- Add `order_all` to the Magos's cult rules in `src/main/cults/cultRules.ts`: use it for an order every acolyte must follow, and `send_agent_message` for one acolyte.
- Errors are typed codes the Magos can act on: `cap_reached`, `model_unavailable`, `tier_reason_required`, `run_paused`, `run_ending`, `name_taken`, `folder_not_tracked`, `no_acolytes`, `unauthorized`.

## Source locations
- `src/core/commands/chatNaming.ts`, `src/core/commands/index.ts`, `src/core/commands/capabilities.ts` (`COMMAND_CAPABILITIES`), `src/core/authz.ts`, `src/shared/agents/chatNaming.ts` (control schemas), `src/core/desktop/desktopClient.ts`, `src/main/naming/controlPipe.ts`.
- `src/main/cults/cultSupervisor.ts`, `src/main/cults/ompModels.ts`, `src/main/cults/cultRules.ts`, `src/main/cults/cultStore.ts` (`cult_events`); the comms mailbox send service (the investigation names the merged file).
- New: `src/core/commands/cults.ts`, `src/shared/cults/cultControl.ts`.

## Tests
- `src/core/commands/cults.test.ts`: input schemas and alias registration.
- `src/main/cults/cultControl.test.ts`, through the real pipe server with fake supervisor state:
  - a non-member is refused;
  - an acolyte calling a Magos-only command is refused;
  - default model is the cheapest;
  - an unknown model is refused with the list;
  - a higher tier without a reason is refused;
  - summoning at the cap is refused;
  - each petition kind is validated (a folder must be tracked);
  - a taken name is refused and a missing name is generated;
  - the chronicle size limit holds;
  - `order_all` delivers exactly one message to each live acolyte, records one `order_all` event with matching message ids, and is refused when paused, when ending, when there are no acolytes, and for an acolyte caller.
- Extend `src/core/commands/capabilities.test.ts`.


