## Context
Epic Cults, revision 3 (read the epic intent, section "The chamber"). The chamber is a side-view room. The Magos stands at a helm on the right edge, consoles stand on the floor, a teleport pad sits near the helm, and a blast door is at the left edge. This ticket is the **pure, seeded simulation** behind the scene, with no React and no DOM. The rendering tickets draw what it computes.

Reuse `src/renderer/src/mascot/motion.ts`. Its seeded engine already makes the mascot wander, run, jump, climb, stumble and drill over rectangles (`MotionRect` "tickets"). In the chamber, the console tops and the helm are those rectangles. Do not change the GraphMascot's behaviour: if motion.ts needs an extension, make it opt-in and keep `motion.test.ts` passing unchanged.

## Change
All of this goes in `src/renderer/src/cults/chamber/`.
- `layout.ts`: `chamberLayout(size, props, headcount)` returns:
  - the floor line, the helm rectangle flush with the right edge, the door at the left edge, the teleport pad left of the helm, the viewscreen rectangle in the back wall's upper middle third, and up to 6 consoles spread evenly between door and pad;
  - a sprite scale: 1 for up to 6 acolytes, falling linearly to 0.6 at 24.
  Prop metrics come in as a parameter shaped like the art ticket's `props.json` (`standTop`, `window`, `doorway`); tests use fixtures.
- `chamberState.ts`:
  - `createChamber(seed)`, `applyChamberEvent(state, event, layout)` and `stepChamber(state, dtMs, layout)`, with one step for all actors.
  - Events: `memberJoined{id}` (beam-in at the pad), `memberLeft{id}` (walk out the door, then removed), `working{id, on}`, `bubble{id, text}`, `orderSent{to: id | 'all', orderId}`, `reportSent{from}`, `peerMail{from, to}`, `magosBusy{on}`, `petitionPending{on}`, `runState{'idle'|'running'|'paused'|'ending'|'ended'|'killed'}` and `lastMinute{on}`.
  - Acolyte modes:
    - arriving, then wandering: the motion engine with console and helm rects as platforms;
    - working: route to its assigned console and loop `type`; with more workers than consoles, the extras `drill` on the floor;
    - saluting: interrupt, face the helm, play the `salute` one-shot, then resume the previous mode;
    - leaving, then gone.
  - Magos: one action at a time with priority chronicle > petition > order_all > order_one > summon > speak > idle. One-shots take their duration from injected clip timings (fps × frames) and return to idle or speak.
  - Bubbles: one per actor; shown for at least 2.5 s and at most 6 s; text capped at 60 characters with an ellipsis; newer text replaces older only after the minimum time.
  - Theatrics:
    - paused: `stepChamber` returns the state unchanged (positions, poses, effects and timers all frozen) and sets `stasis`;
    - running again: continues from the same poses;
    - ending: each acolyte sends a report packet, then marches to the door and is removed; the Magos plays chronicle; `lightsDim` is set once the last acolyte is gone;
    - killed: every acolyte is removed at once, and `blackout` and sparks are set;
    - lastMinute: sets `warning`.
- `effects.ts`:
  - a packet travels on an arc from source to target in 600 to 1200 ms, in proportion to distance, and triggers the recipient's reaction on arrival;
  - a noosphere ring expands from the helm across the room, and each acolyte salutes when the ring reaches it;
  - also beam-in columns and sparks.
- `staticChamber(state, layout)`, for reduced motion: Magos at the helm, working acolytes at consoles, the others in an even row on the floor, with no travel and no effects, but the same bubbles and flags.
- Clip timings and prop metrics are parameters, so this ticket depends on no art.

## Source locations
- `src/renderer/src/mascot/motion.ts` (`createMotion`, `stepMotion`, `MotionRect`, `MotionSurfaces`), `motion.test.ts`.
- `src/renderer/src/mascot/sprite.ts` (atlas fps and frame counts, for the clip-timing shape).
- `src/renderer/src/mascot/GraphMascot.tsx` (how a frame loop calls the engine).
- New: `src/renderer/src/cults/chamber/layout.ts`, `chamberState.ts`, `effects.ts`, and their tests.

## Tests
- `layout.test.ts`: the helm is flush right; consoles are between door and pad without overlap at 800, 1280 and 1920 px; the scale is 1 at 6, 0.6 at 24, and linear between.
- `chamberState.test.ts`:
  - a targeted order sends one packet to that acolyte only, which salutes on arrival and then resumes its previous mode;
  - `order all` makes every acolyte salute exactly once, in order of distance from the helm;
  - a report sends a packet to the Magos, which then plays speak;
  - a working acolyte reaches its console and types; the 7th worker drills;
  - while paused, 10 s of steps change nothing, and resume continues identically to a run with no pause;
  - in ending, every acolyte reports, exits the door and is removed, then `lightsDim` is set;
  - killed removes all at once and sets `blackout`;
  - the same seed and the same events give identical states;
  - the bubble timing rules hold.
- `effects.test.ts`: packet duration bounds and ring arrival order.
- `motion.test.ts` passes unchanged.


