## Context
Epic Cults, revision 3 (read the epic intent, sections "Orders and reports" and "Run-state theatrics"). The chamber logic (`chamberState.ts`, `effects.ts`) already computes bubbles, packets, rings, beam-ins, sparks and the `stasis`, `lightsDim`, `blackout` and `warning` flags. The scene ticket renders the actors and leaves an effects layer in `CultChamber.tsx`. This ticket draws the rest. All effects are code-drawn (CSS/SVG), with no new art.

## Change
- `src/renderer/src/cults/chamber/SpeechBubble.tsx`:
  - a rounded bubble above the actor's head with a tail, its border in the member colour (the Magos gets brass);
  - **plain text only** (a React text node, never HTML or Markdown);
  - kept inside the room: it flips side near an edge and stacks upward when bubbles would overlap.
- `src/renderer/src/cults/chamber/ChamberEffects.tsx`:
  - packet: a glowing green binharic dot with a short fading trail along the computed arc;
  - noosphere ring: an expanding ellipse from the helm across the floor plane;
  - beam-in: a light column on the pad that fades;
  - sparks: a short particle burst.
- Theatrics on the scene root:
  - `stasis`: grayscale and a dimmed overlay with a "STASIS" plate;
  - `lightsDim`: slow darkening;
  - `blackout`: instant black, with a few sparks;
  - `warning`: pulsing red edge lights.
- Reduced motion: no packets, rings, beams or pulses. A targeted order instead briefly outlines the recipient's name plate; order all outlines every plate. Bubbles and the stasis, dim and blackout states still render, statically.
- Extend `preview/cults/chamber.tsx` so every button visibly triggers its effect.

## Source locations
- `src/renderer/src/cults/chamber/CultChamber.tsx`, `chamberState.ts`, `effects.ts`, `chamber.css` (from earlier tickets).
- `src/renderer/src/mascot/motionGuards.ts` (`useMotionPreference`).
- New: `ChamberEffects.tsx`, `SpeechBubble.tsx`, and their tests.

## Tests
