## Context
Epic Cults, revision 3 (read the epic intent, section "The chamber"). The pieces exist by now:
- the chamber (`CultChamber`, with effects);
- the Cult page with its room slot, roster, inspector, petition banner and comms tabs;
- run snapshots with member activity (`cults:event`);
- the pipeline (`useCultPipeline`, with `order_all` grouping);
- the `ShrinePanel`.
This ticket connects them, so a real run plays in the room.

## Change
- `src/renderer/src/cults/chamber/chamberFeed.ts` (pure) turns consecutive run snapshots and new pipeline entries into chamber events:
  - member added or removed → `memberJoined`/`memberLeft`;
  - working changes → `working`;
  - activity changes → `bubble`;
  - Magos busy → `magosBusy`;
  - any pending petition → `petitionPending`;
  - run state → `runState`;
  - under 60 s of a timed run left → `lastMinute`;
  - pipeline: Magos to one acolyte → `orderSent{to}` plus a `bubble` with the mail's first line; an `order_all` group → one `orderSent{to:'all'}`; acolyte to Magos → `reportSent`; acolyte to acolyte → `peerMail`;
  - idempotent by snapshot revision and pipeline sequence: repeated or overlapping pages and polls never animate twice; entries that existed before mount are never replayed; reopening the page starts from the current state.
- `src/renderer/src/cults/chamber/bubbleLines.ts` (pure) phrases activity in a Mechanicus voice:
  - a template table by tool kind, e.g. "Sanctifying {target}" for edit/write, "Consulting the archive: {target}" for read, "Invoking the rite of {target}" for shell, "Scrying the noosphere for {target}" for search;
  - a plain fallback, "Using {tool}";
  - a mail line: the first non-empty line, at most 60 characters;
  - at least 12 seeded idle quips (for example, "Praise the Omnissiah", "*whirr*", "Who touched my cogitator?"), shown after 20 s idle and at most once every 30 s per acolyte;
  - all output is plain text.
- Mount `CultChamber` in the Cult page's room slot:
  - members get `memberHue` from `src/renderer/src/cults/memberColors.ts` (the same colours as the roster and pipeline);
  - `selectedMemberId` and `onSelectMember` connect to the page's inspector;
  - the viewscreen hosts `ShrinePanel` in its compact mode with Enlarge; with no offering, it shows a static "No offering yet" glyph;
  - with no active run, the room shows lights off and no actors.
- Past runs show no chamber; they keep the drawer and the read-only pipeline.

## Source locations
- `src/renderer/src/cults/CultPage.tsx` (room slot, inspector), `src/renderer/src/cults/useCults.ts`, `src/renderer/src/cults/memberColors.ts`.
- `src/renderer/src/cults/PipelinePanel.tsx` and `useCultPipeline` (pipeline ticket), `src/renderer/src/cults/ShrinePanel.tsx` (Shrine ticket).
- `src/renderer/src/cults/chamber/` (chamber tickets), `src/shared/cults/cultApi.ts` (snapshot and pipeline entry types).
- New: `chamberFeed.ts`, `bubbleLines.ts`, and their tests.

## Tests
- `chamberFeed.test.ts`:
  - each mapping above;
  - an `order_all` group gives exactly one `orderSent{to:'all'}`;
  - the same snapshot or page twice gives no new events;
  - entries before mount are not replayed;
  - `lastMinute` turns on at under 60 s and never for Unlimited runs.
- `bubbleLines.test.ts`: the template for each tool kind, the fallback, the 60-character cap, the quip throttling, and text with markup staying literal.
- `CultPage.chamber.test.tsx`:
  - clicking a sprite opens the inspector for that member;
  - an acolyte's robe hue equals its pipeline and roster colour;
  - no active run shows the dark room;
  - the Shrine renders in the viewscreen.


