## Context
The standard worker catalog cannot anticipate every domain. After the base commands and Plan Forge gate exist, add a bounded Magos-only mechanism for a run-specific specialist. It must not become a permission or model-escalation path.

## Change
Create `src/main/cults/dynamicWorkerTypes.ts` and extend the cult control registry:
- Magos-only `create_worker_type {name, description, mission, rationale, requiredForConclusion?}`; main generates the id and persists through `cultStore`;
- Magos-only `list_worker_types {}` and `retire_worker_type {workerTypeId, reason}`;
- `summon_acolyte` accepts either a definition slot or active run worker-type id and resolves the contract in main;
- enforce normalized uniqueness, built-in collision checks, field limits, 24-type ceiling, active-run state and typed errors (`worker_type_name_taken`, `worker_type_limit`, `worker_type_required`, `worker_type_assigned`, `worker_type_unknown`);
- created types add no capability, grant, folder, Save right, model or tier. Existing cap and petition rules apply to the summoned acolyte;
- required types cannot retire; optional types retire only before assignment; all mutations append cult events;
- rules/native Skitarii tools expose the three commands only to the Magos.

## Source locations
- Planned `src/shared/cults/archetypes.ts`, `src/main/cults/cultStore.ts`, `src/main/cults/cultSupervisor.ts`, `src/shared/cults/cultControl.ts`, `src/core/commands/cults.ts`, `src/main/cults/cultRules.ts`.
- `src/core/commands/capabilities.ts`, `src/core/authz.ts`, `resources/skitarii/extension/index.ts`.
- New: `src/main/cults/dynamicWorkerTypes.ts`, `src/main/cults/dynamicWorkerTypes.test.ts`.

## Tests
`dynamicWorkerTypes.test.ts` covers create/list/retire/inject, built-in and duplicate collisions, field and count limits, caller authority, required/assigned retirement, run state, unchanged grants/models, cap refusal and event history. Extend control registry and native tool tests.

